{"id":"70a60076aaa1fb8eb9444c45ee3ad5e5fb740193","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"70a60076aaa1fb8eb9444c45ee3ad5e5fb740193","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"api/envoy/config/route/v3/route_components.proto","lines":["@@ -2807,7 +2807,11 @@ message RateLimit {","   // requests based on the action with this field set to true. Users should ensure that the rate limit is enforced by the actions","   // applied on the request path, i.e. the ones with this field set to false.","   //","-  // Currently, this is only supported by the HTTP global rate filter.","+  // Supported by HTTP global rate limiting. HTTP local rate limiting supports this only for the","+  // filter's embedded ``rate_limits``, including per-route ``typed_per_filter_config``, and ignores it","+  // for route and virtual-host ``rate_limits``. Local completion charges matching descriptor buckets","+  // in full, overdrawing them by up to one bucket of tokens when the usage exceeds the remaining","+  // budget; the default bucket is consumed only on requests.","   bool apply_on_stream_done = 6;"," ","   // Descriptor level X-RateLimit headers options which may override the filter level setting."],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"api/envoy/extensions/filters/http/local_ratelimit/v3/local_rate_limit.proto","lines":["@@ -180,6 +180,11 @@ message LocalRateLimit {","   //   2. :ref:`dynamic metadata <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.Action.dynamic_metadata>`.","   //   3. :ref:`disable_key <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.disable_key>`.","   //   4. :ref:`override limit <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.limit>`.","+  //","+  //   :ref:`apply_on_stream_done <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.apply_on_stream_done>`","+  //   updates descriptor buckets from response context at completion without enforcing the current","+  //   request, in both the filter-level and per-route configuration. Use request-path actions for the","+  //   same descriptor to enforce subsequent requests.","   repeated config.route.v3.RateLimit rate_limits = 17;"," ","   // Specifies the max dynamic descriptors kept in the cache for a particular wildcard descriptor"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/new_features/local_ratelimit__apply-on-stream-done.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+Added HTTP local rate limit completion accounting for embedded ``rate_limits`` with","+:ref:`apply_on_stream_done <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.apply_on_stream_done>`,","+in both the filter-level and per-route configuration. These actions update matching descriptor","+token buckets when the stream completes and remain skipped on the request path. The default local","+token bucket continues to apply only on the request path. Route and virtual-host rate limit entries","+are unchanged and continue to apply on the request path."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/root/configuration/http/http_filters/local_rate_limit_filter.rst","lines":["@@ -151,6 +151,67 @@ path, then 10 req/min are allowed. But if they come from a downstream service"," cluster \"foo\" for \"/foo/bar2\" path, then 100 req/min are allowed. Otherwise,"," 1000 req/min are allowed."," ","+Accounting for usage when a stream completes","+--------------------------------------------","+","+Set :ref:`apply_on_stream_done <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.apply_on_stream_done>`","+on an embedded ``rate_limits`` action to update local descriptor token buckets when the stream completes.","+This allows :ref:`hits_addend <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.RateLimit.hits_addend>` in the","+filter's ``rate_limits`` to use response headers or final stream information, such as","+``%RESP(x-usage)%`` or ``%BYTES_SENT%``.","+","+This works in both the filter-level configuration and the per-route configuration in","+:ref:`typed_per_filter_config <envoy_v3_api_field_config.route.v3.Route.typed_per_filter_config>`.","+The local rate limit filter ignores ``apply_on_stream_done`` on route and virtual-host","+``rate_limits``; those entries continue to apply on the request path.","+","+Example using embedded ``rate_limits``:","+","+.. code-block:: yaml","+","+  rate_limits:","+  - actions:","+    - generic_key:","+        descriptor_key: usage","+        descriptor_value: service","+  - actions:","+    - generic_key:","+        descriptor_key: usage","+        descriptor_value: service","+    apply_on_stream_done: true","+    hits_addend:","+      format: \"%RESP(x-usage)%\"","+","+The first action enforces the budget and consumes one token on the request path. The second","+charges additional usage reported in the ``x-usage`` response header when the stream completes.","+Both actions must match a configured local descriptor. Completion actions update every matching","+descriptor bucket without blocking the completed request. Usage exceeding the remaining budget","+overdraws the bucket: it borrows future tokens, and later requests are rejected until the refill","+repays the debt. The debt is capped at the bucket's ``max_tokens``, and usage beyond the cap is","+dropped. The default token bucket is consumed only on the request path.","+Missing, empty or invalid formatted usage does not generate a descriptor and logs a warning.","+Negative hits addends refund tokens using the existing local descriptor behavior.","+","+With ``local_cluster_rate_limit``, positive charges are divided by the local cluster's token share","+factor, while refunds add the specified token count without scaling. This matches request-path","+refund behavior. A charge and refund with the same addend do not cancel when the share factor is","+less than one.","+","+Request and completion actions share the same bounded cache for wildcard descriptors. A value","+first seen at completion creates a bucket and can evict another bucket, including one used for","+request enforcement. Revisiting an evicted value creates a fresh bucket with its initial budget.","+Size ``max_dynamic_descriptors`` for the combined cardinality of request and completion values.","+","+Completion accounting works with process-wide and per-connection buckets. Request counters and","+rate limit response headers reflect the request-path decision; completion accounting does not","+change the response or increment request counters again.","+","+As with the global rate limit filter, completion actions also run when the request was rejected","+by the rate limit filter. Stream information such as ``%BYTES_SENT%`` includes usage from a local","+rate limit response. To account for upstream-reported usage, use a response header such as","+``%RESP(x-usage)%`` that is present only when the upstream reports a cost. A missing header","+drops the descriptor and logs a warning.","+"," Statistics"," ----------"," "],"additions":61,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ RateLimitTokenBucket::RateLimitTokenBucket(uint64_t max_tokens, uint64_t tokens_","       fill_interval_(fill_interval), shadow_mode_(shadow_mode),","       preserve_one_request_(Runtime::runtimeFeatureEnabled(","           \"envoy.reloadable_features.local_ratelimit_local_cluster_preserve_one_request\")) {}","-bool RateLimitTokenBucket::consume(double factor, uint64_t to_consume) {","+bool RateLimitTokenBucket::consume(double factor, uint64_t to_consume, bool overdraft) {","   ASSERT(!(factor <= 0.0 || factor > 1.0));","   const double max_tokens = token_bucket_.maxTokens();","   const double tokens = to_consume / factor;","@@ -99,7 +99,14 @@ bool RateLimitTokenBucket::consume(double factor, uint64_t to_consume) {","   const double threshold = preserve_one_request_ && max_tokens > 0 && to_consume <= max_tokens","                                ? std::min(tokens, max_tokens)","                                : tokens;","-  auto cb = [tokens, threshold](double total) { return total < threshold ? 0.0 : tokens; };","+  auto cb = [tokens, threshold, overdraft, max_tokens](double total) {","+    if (overdraft) {","+      // Borrow future tokens when the bucket is short, but by at most max_tokens, so a single","+      // large cost can't block the bucket indefinitely.","+      return std::max(0.0, std::min(tokens, total + max_tokens));","+    }","+    return total >= threshold ? tokens : 0.0;","+  };","   return token_bucket_.consume(cb) != 0.0;"," }"," ","@@ -193,6 +200,29 @@ LocalRateLimiterImpl::LocalRateLimiterImpl("," "," LocalRateLimiterImpl::~LocalRateLimiterImpl() = default;"," ","+RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr","+LocalRateLimiterImpl::getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor& descriptor) {","+  auto iter = descriptors_.find(descriptor);","+  return iter != descriptors_.end() ? iter->second : dynamic_descriptors_.getBucket(descriptor);","+}","+","+void LocalRateLimiterImpl::consumeDescriptors(","+    absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptors) {","+  const double share_factor =","+      share_provider_ != nullptr ? share_provider_->getTokensShareFactor() : 1.0;","+  for (const auto& descriptor : request_descriptors) {","+    auto bucket = getBucket(descriptor);","+    if (bucket == nullptr) {","+      continue;","+    }","+    if (descriptor.is_negative_hits_ && descriptor.hits_addend_.has_value()) {","+      bucket->refill(descriptor.hits_addend_.value());","+    } else {","+      bucket->consume(share_factor, descriptor.hits_addend_.value_or(1), /*overdraft=*/true);","+    }","+  }","+}","+"," struct MatchResult {","   RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr token_bucket;","   std::reference_wrapper<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptor;","@@ -207,14 +237,9 @@ LocalRateLimiterImpl::requestAllowed(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> req"," ","   // Find all matched descriptors.","   for (const auto& request_descriptor : request_descriptors) {","-    auto iter = descriptors_.find(request_descriptor);","-    if (iter != descriptors_.end()) {","-      matched_results.push_back(MatchResult{iter->second, request_descriptor});","-    } else {","-      auto token_bucket = dynamic_descriptors_.getBucket(request_descriptor);","-      if (token_bucket != nullptr) {","-        matched_results.push_back(MatchResult{token_bucket, request_descriptor});","-      }","+    auto token_bucket = getBucket(request_descriptor);","+    if (token_bucket != nullptr) {","+      matched_results.push_back(MatchResult{std::move(token_bucket), request_descriptor});","     }","   }"," ","@@ -345,9 +370,9 @@ void DynamicDescriptorMap::addDescriptor(const RateLimit::LocalDescriptor& confi"," }"," "," RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr","-DynamicDescriptorMap::getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor request_descriptor) {","+DynamicDescriptorMap::getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor& request_descriptor) {","   for (const auto& pair : config_descriptors_) {","-    auto config_descriptor = pair.first;","+    const auto& config_descriptor = pair.first;","     if (!matchDescriptorEntries(request_descriptor.entries_, config_descriptor.entries_)) {","       continue;","     }"],"additions":37,"deletions":12,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit_impl.h","lines":["@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ class DynamicDescriptorMap : public Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::rate_limit_quot","   void addDescriptor(const RateLimit::LocalDescriptor& descriptor,","                      DynamicDescriptorSharedPtr dynamic_descriptor);","   // pass request_descriptors to the dynamic descriptor set to get the token bucket.","-  RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor);","+  RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor&);"," "," private:","   bool matchDescriptorEntries(const std::vector<RateLimit::DescriptorEntry>& request_entries,","@@ -111,7 +111,10 @@ class RateLimitTokenBucket : public TokenBucketContext,","                        bool shadow_mode);"," ","   // RateLimitTokenBucket","-  bool consume(double factor = 1.0, uint64_t tokens = 1);","+  // With overdraft, the cost is consumed even when the bucket is short, and the bucket can go","+  // below zero by at most max_tokens. Later requests wait until the refill repays the debt.","+  // Returns false only when the bucket is already at the debt cap.","+  bool consume(double factor = 1.0, uint64_t tokens = 1, bool overdraft = false);","   // Refill tokens back to the bucket, capped at max_tokens.","   void refill(uint64_t tokens);","   double fillRate() const { return token_bucket_.fillRate(); }","@@ -151,7 +154,12 @@ class LocalRateLimiterImpl : public Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::local_rate_limi","   LocalRateLimiter::Result","   requestAllowed(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptors) override;"," ","+  // Account for completed descriptor usage without enforcement. Usage beyond the remaining budget","+  // overdraws the bucket. The default bucket is consumed only on the request path.","+  void consumeDescriptors(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptors);","+"," private:","+  RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr getBucket(const RateLimit::Descriptor& descriptor);","   RateLimitTokenBucketSharedPtr default_token_bucket_;"," ","   TimeSource& time_source_;"],"additions":10,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit.cc","lines":["@@ -60,6 +60,9 @@ FilterConfig::FilterConfig(","               : std::nullopt),","       stage_(static_cast<uint64_t>(config.stage())),","       has_descriptors_(!config.descriptors().empty()),","+      has_stream_done_actions_(","+          std::any_of(config.rate_limits().begin(), config.rate_limits().end(),","+                      [](const auto& rate_limit) { return rate_limit.apply_on_stream_done(); })),","       enable_x_rate_limit_headers_(config.enable_x_ratelimit_headers() ==","                                    envoy::extensions::common::ratelimit::v3::DRAFT_VERSION_03),","       enable_retry_after_header_(config.enable_retry_after_header() &&","@@ -164,6 +167,9 @@ bool FilterConfig::enforced() const {","   return filter_enforced_.has_value() ? filter_enforced_->enabled() : false;"," }"," ","+Filter::Filter(FilterConfigSharedPtr config)","+    : config_(std::move(config)), used_config_(config_.get()) {}","+"," Http::FilterHeadersStatus Filter::decodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers, bool) {","   const auto* route_config =","       Http::Utility::resolveMostSpecificPerFilterConfig<FilterConfig>(decoder_callbacks_);","@@ -176,7 +182,8 @@ Http::FilterHeadersStatus Filter::decodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers,","     used_config_ = route_config; // Overwrite the used configuration.","   }"," ","-  if (!used_config_->enabled()) {","+  rate_limit_enabled_ = used_config_->enabled();","+  if (!rate_limit_enabled_) {","     return Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue;","   }"," ","@@ -185,7 +192,9 @@ Http::FilterHeadersStatus Filter::decodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers,","   std::vector<RateLimit::Descriptor> descriptors;","   if (used_config_->hasDescriptors()) {","     if (used_config_->hasRateLimitConfigs()) {","-      used_config_->populateDescriptors(headers, decoder_callbacks_->streamInfo(), descriptors);","+      used_config_->populateDescriptors(headers, /*response_headers=*/nullptr,","+                                        decoder_callbacks_->streamInfo(), descriptors,","+                                        /*on_stream_done=*/false);","     } else {","       populateDescriptors(descriptors, headers);","     }","@@ -265,6 +274,32 @@ Http::FilterHeadersStatus Filter::encodeHeaders(Http::ResponseHeaderMap& headers","   return Http::FilterHeadersStatus::Continue;"," }"," ","+void Filter::onDestroy() {","+  // Completion accounting needs local descriptors and embedded apply_on_stream_done rate limits.","+  if (!rate_limit_enabled_ || !used_config_->hasDescriptors() ||","+      !used_config_->hasStreamDoneActions()) {","+    return;","+  }","+  // Read the headers from the stream rather than keeping references to them.","+  const auto request_headers = decoder_callbacks_->requestHeaders();","+  if (!request_headers.has_value()) {","+    return;","+  }","+  const auto response_headers = decoder_callbacks_->responseHeaders();","+  std::vector<RateLimit::Descriptor> descriptors;","+  used_config_->populateDescriptors(*request_headers, response_headers.ptr(),","+                                    decoder_callbacks_->streamInfo(), descriptors,","+                                    /*on_stream_done=*/true);","+  if (descriptors.empty()) {","+    return;","+  }","+  if (used_config_->rateLimitPerConnection()) {","+    getPerConnectionRateLimiter().consumeDescriptors(descriptors);","+  } else {","+    used_config_->consumeDescriptors(descriptors);","+  }","+}","+"," Filters::Common::LocalRateLimit::LocalRateLimiterImpl::Result"," Filter::requestAllowed(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptors) {","   return used_config_->rateLimitPerConnection()"],"additions":37,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit.h","lines":["@@ -94,6 +94,9 @@ class FilterConfig : public Router::RouteSpecificFilterConfig,","   Runtime::Loader& runtime() { return runtime_; }","   Filters::Common::LocalRateLimit::LocalRateLimiter::Result","   requestAllowed(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> request_descriptors) const;","+  void consumeDescriptors(absl::Span<const RateLimit::Descriptor> descriptors) const {","+    rate_limiter_->consumeDescriptors(descriptors);","+  }","   bool enabled() const;","   bool enforced() const;","   LocalRateLimitStats& stats() const { return stats_; }","@@ -102,6 +105,7 @@ class FilterConfig : public Router::RouteSpecificFilterConfig,","   Http::Code status() const { return status_; }","   uint64_t stage() const { return stage_; }","   bool hasDescriptors() const { return has_descriptors_; }","+  bool hasStreamDoneActions() const { return has_stream_done_actions_; }","   const std::chrono::milliseconds& fillInterval() const { return fill_interval_; }","   uint32_t maxTokens() const { return max_tokens_; }","   uint32_t tokensPerFill() const { return tokens_per_fill_; }","@@ -128,13 +132,13 @@ class FilterConfig : public Router::RouteSpecificFilterConfig,","   }"," ","   void populateDescriptors(const Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers,","+                           const Http::ResponseHeaderMap* response_headers,","                            const StreamInfo::StreamInfo& info,","-                           Filters::Common::RateLimit::RateLimitDescriptors& descriptors) const {","+                           Filters::Common::RateLimit::RateLimitDescriptors& descriptors,","+                           bool on_stream_done) const {","     ASSERT(rate_limit_config_ != nullptr);","-    // Local rate limiting runs on the decode path only; no response headers are available to the","-    // formatter (and %RESP()% in hits_addend.format resolves empty, as before).","-    rate_limit_config_->populateDescriptors(headers, /*response_headers=*/nullptr, info,","-                                            local_info_.clusterName(), descriptors);","+    rate_limit_config_->populateDescriptors(headers, response_headers, info,","+                                            local_info_.clusterName(), descriptors, on_stream_done);","   }"," "," private:","@@ -172,6 +176,7 @@ class FilterConfig : public Router::RouteSpecificFilterConfig,","   Router::HeaderParserPtr request_headers_parser_;","   const uint64_t stage_;","   const bool has_descriptors_;","+  const bool has_stream_done_actions_;","   const bool enable_x_rate_limit_headers_;","   const bool enable_retry_after_header_ = false;","   const envoy::extensions::common::ratelimit::v3::VhRateLimitsOptions vh_rate_limits_;","@@ -187,7 +192,10 @@ using FilterConfigSharedPtr = std::shared_ptr<FilterConfig>;","  */"," class Filter : public Http::PassThroughFilter, Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::filter> {"," public:","-  Filter(FilterConfigSharedPtr config) : config_(config), used_config_(config_.get()) {}","+  Filter(FilterConfigSharedPtr config);","+","+  // Http::StreamFilterBase","+  void onDestroy() override;"," ","   // Http::StreamDecoderFilter","   Http::FilterHeadersStatus decodeHeaders(Http::RequestHeaderMap& headers,","@@ -224,6 +232,8 @@ class Filter : public Http::PassThroughFilter, Logger::Loggable<Logger::Id::filt","   const FilterConfig* used_config_{};","   std::shared_ptr<const Filters::Common::LocalRateLimit::TokenBucketContext> token_bucket_context_;","   RateLimit::XRateLimitOption x_ratelimit_option_{};","+  // Whether decodeHeaders() ran with the filter enabled. Completion accounting respects it.","+  bool rate_limit_enabled_{false};"," ","   VhRateLimitOptions vh_rate_limits_;"," };"],"additions":16,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/BUILD","lines":["@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@ envoy_cc_test(","     srcs = [\"local_ratelimit_test.cc\"],","     rbe_pool = \"linux_x64_small\",","     deps = [","+        \"//envoy/common:time_interface\",","         \"//source/common/singleton:manager_impl_lib\",","         \"//source/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit:local_ratelimit_lib\",","         \"//test/mocks/event:event_mocks\",","         \"//test/mocks/upstream:cluster_manager_mocks\",","         \"//test/mocks/upstream:cluster_priority_set_mocks\",","+        \"//test/test_common:simulated_time_system_lib\",","         \"//test/test_common:test_runtime_lib\",","         \"//test/test_common:utility_lib\",","     ],"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit_test.cc","lines":["@@ -1,9 +1,12 @@","+#include \"envoy/common/time.h\"","+"," #include \"source/common/singleton/manager_impl.h\""," #include \"source/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit_impl.h\""," "," #include \"test/mocks/event/mocks.h\""," #include \"test/mocks/upstream/cluster_manager.h\""," #include \"test/mocks/upstream/cluster_priority_set.h\"","+#include \"test/test_common/simulated_time_system.h\""," #include \"test/test_common/test_runtime.h\""," #include \"test/test_common/thread_factory_for_test.h\""," #include \"test/test_common/utility.h\"","@@ -726,6 +729,226 @@ TEST_F(LocalRateLimiterDescriptorImplTest, AtomicTokenBucketMultipleTokensPerFil","   EXPECT_FALSE(rate_limiter_->requestAllowed(descriptor_).allowed);"," }"," ","+class MockRateLimitTimeSource : public TimeSource {","+public:","+  MOCK_METHOD(SystemTime, systemTime, (), (override));","+  MOCK_METHOD(MonotonicTime, monotonicTime, (), (override));","+};","+","+TEST(RateLimitTokenBucketTest, OverdraftChargesFullCostBeyondRemainingTokens) {","+  testing::StrictMock<MockRateLimitTimeSource> time_source;","+  const MonotonicTime start(std::chrono::seconds(10));","+  testing::InSequence sequence;","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  RateLimitTokenBucket bucket(3, 1, std::chrono::milliseconds(1000), time_source, false);","+","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  EXPECT_FALSE(bucket.consume(1.0, 5));","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume(1.0, 5, /*overdraft=*/true));","+","+  // Two tokens are owed, so the bucket stays empty until three seconds of refill.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillRepeatedly(Return(start + std::chrono::seconds(2)));","+  EXPECT_EQ(0, bucket.remainingTokens());","+  EXPECT_FALSE(bucket.consume());","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start + std::chrono::seconds(3)));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume());","+}","+","+TEST(RateLimitTokenBucketTest, OverdraftDebtIsCappedAtMaxTokens) {","+  testing::StrictMock<MockRateLimitTimeSource> time_source;","+  const MonotonicTime start(std::chrono::seconds(10));","+  testing::InSequence sequence;","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  RateLimitTokenBucket bucket(2, 1, std::chrono::milliseconds(1000), time_source, false);","+","+  // A cost far beyond the bucket overdraws it by only max_tokens.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume(1.0, 1000, /*overdraft=*/true));","+  // At the cap, further overdrafts add no debt.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start));","+  EXPECT_FALSE(bucket.consume(1.0, 1, /*overdraft=*/true));","+","+  // Two tokens are owed, so the bucket recovers after three seconds instead of ~1000.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillRepeatedly(Return(start + std::chrono::seconds(2)));","+  EXPECT_EQ(0, bucket.remainingTokens());","+  EXPECT_FALSE(bucket.consume());","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(start + std::chrono::seconds(3)));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume());","+}","+","+TEST(RateLimitTokenBucketTest, OverdraftKeepsFullCostAfterInterleavedDrain) {","+  testing::StrictMock<MockRateLimitTimeSource> time_source;","+  const MonotonicTime earlier(std::chrono::seconds(10));","+  const MonotonicTime later = earlier + std::chrono::seconds(1);","+  testing::InSequence sequence;","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(earlier));","+  RateLimitTokenBucket bucket(2, 1, std::chrono::milliseconds(1000), time_source, false);","+","+  // Drain at a later time before returning this caller's earlier time sample.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(testing::Invoke([&]() {","+    EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume(1.0, 2));","+    return earlier;","+  }));","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(later));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume(1.0, 1, /*overdraft=*/true));","+","+  // The delayed charge is not lost or refunded: the bucket owes one token beyond the drain.","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillRepeatedly(Return(later + std::chrono::seconds(1)));","+  EXPECT_EQ(0, bucket.remainingTokens());","+  EXPECT_FALSE(bucket.consume());","+  EXPECT_CALL(time_source, monotonicTime()).WillOnce(Return(later + std::chrono::seconds(2)));","+  EXPECT_TRUE(bucket.consume());","+}","+","+class CompletedUsageTest : public Event::TestUsingSimulatedTime,","+                           public LocalRateLimiterDescriptorImplTest {};","+","+TEST_F(CompletedUsageTest, CompletedUsageConsumesAllMatchingBuckets) {","+  TestUtility::loadFromYaml(fmt::format(single_descriptor_config_yaml, 2, 1, \"1000s\"),","+                            *descriptors_.Add());","+  TestUtility::loadFromYaml(fmt::format(multiple_descriptor_config_yaml, 5, 1, \"1000s\"),","+                            *descriptors_.Add());","+  initializeWithAtomicTokenBucketDescriptor(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000000), 10, 1);","+  std::vector<RateLimit::Descriptor> descriptors{descriptor_[0], descriptor2_[0]};","+  descriptors[0].hits_addend_ = 3;","+  descriptors[1].hits_addend_ = 3;","+  rate_limiter_->consumeDescriptors(descriptors);","+  // Over-budget usage overdraws the first bucket without skipping the second.","+  EXPECT_FALSE(rate_limiter_->requestAllowed(descriptor_).allowed);","+  auto result = rate_limiter_->requestAllowed(descriptor2_);","+  EXPECT_TRUE(result.allowed);","+  EXPECT_EQ(1, result.token_bucket_context->remainingTokens());","+}","+","+TEST_F(CompletedUsageTest, CompletedUsageDoesNotConsumeDefaultBucket) {","+  TestUtility::loadFromYaml(fmt::format(single_descriptor_config_yaml, 5, 1, \"1000s\"),","+                            *descriptors_.Add());","+  initializeWithAtomicTokenBucketDescriptor(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000000), 1, 1);","+  rate_limiter_->consumeDescriptors({});","+  std::vector<RateLimit::Descriptor> unmatched{{{{\"unknown\", \"value\"}}}};","+  ra